course: dictionary
lesson: 6210
title: The prefix mis- means wrongly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A prefix is a small group of letters at the start of a word that changes its meaning. «mis-» means wrongly. So to misspell a word is to spell it wrongly, and to misread is to read it wrongly.
explain: Look at the word parts: mis + spell = misspell. The root «spell» stays the same, and the prefix tells you how it went wrong. When you meet an unknown word that starts with mis-, ask yourself: does this mean wrongly?
explain: Spelling can be tricky, so a dictionary or a spell-checker helps you find the right way. Many people misspell «misspell» too, so check it if you are unsure: it keeps both s's, one from mis- and one from spell.
fact: Misspell is a verb: to spell a word wrongly.
fact: Its forms are misspell, misspells, misspelled or misspelt, and misspelling.
fact: The prefix «mis-» means wrongly, as in misread, misspell and misbehave.
fact: Adding a prefix never changes the spelling of the root word, so mis + spell = misspell, with both s's.
fact: In English lessons, pupils check their work for misspelled words, and spell-checkers can help find them.
exercise: What does the prefix «mis-» mean in misspell? | Before | Again | Under | *Wrongly
exercise: A pupil writes «garden» as «gardon» in a test. What has she done? | *She has misspelled the word | She has previewed the word | She has spelled it under the table | She has redone the word
exercise: Which part of misspell is the root word? | wrongly | misspell | mis | *spell
test: «Many come from Latin, Greek or French, and grown-ups misspell them too.» What does misspell mean here? | To spell again | To read aloud | To spell it in capitals | *To spell wrongly
test: Which word means to read wrongly? | preview | *misread | redo | submarine
exam: Which word is made from mis + spell, keeping both s's? | misspel | dispell | mispell | *misspell
